  "verbalization": "Ammonia is linked to Seborrheic Dermatitis through a series of indications that collectively suggest a potential therapeutic pathway. The evidence shows that Ammonia is associated with Pityriasis Simplex, which in turn is linked to multiple drugs—Chloroxine, Racementhol, and Selenium Sulfide—that all ultimately indicate Seborrheic Dermatitis. These connections imply that Ammonia may influence the development or progression of Seborrheic Dermatitis through a chain of biological effects, possibly involving inflammatory or skin-related mechanisms. The shared indication of Pityriasis Simplex across different drugs suggests a common pathophysiological role, potentially linking Ammonia to skin condition regulation. The presence of multiple drugs with similar indications reinforces the likelihood of a broader biological mechanism, though the exact nature of this mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
